  "methodology": "Other",
  "methodology_other": "•\tAnalysis conducted using a soil water balance approach including global geospatial raster data comprising precipitation, evapotranspiration, rooted soil depth, and water holding capacity. Analysis conducted on seasonal basis to identify accumulated transpiration through growing seasons, to determine crop yields as function of water availability •\tHazard for 2010 generated using current climate conditions using EU-WATCH global reanalysis data (same dataset as river flood). •\tHazard for 2050 generated using simulations of future climate conditions based on five Global Climate Models for RCP6.0 (same dataset as river flood).",
  "name": "mozambique-drought",
  "notes": "Data produced under the ADRF Sub Saharan Africa Risk Profiles project. The project provides also risk data produced, exposure and hazard data used in the analyses.",
